yK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-25T20:59:09-08:00","id":18141,"title":"","content":"King's Raven: care to elaborate on your Hunter: Cults project? I haven't seen it mentioned before, but it sounds fascinating.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-26T02:16:46-08:00","id":18307,"title":"","content":"Gladly.<br /> <br /> As the one word name might inform you Cults' closet counterpart in the Hunter line is Slasher. Just like Slasher is both a book presenting an evocative monster for your PCs to fight and a look at the Hunter's psyche Cults is going to be both an book of evocative cults for your PCs to fight and a look at the organisational psyche of a Compact/Conspiracy. What makes a Compact turn into a Cult, and perhaps more importantly how does a compact resist turning into a Cult?<br /> <br /> My secondary goal is to sort of sell the idea of playing members of actual organisations. I got the impression that Hunter spends a little more time presenting ways for PCs to, for example, be a member of TF:V without having a commander. So I want to readdress the balance by presenting the other side of the argument: of why being part of an military chain of command is a fun concept.<br /> <br /> It turns out that these goals are <i>hard </i>but I'm I working on it (so's Flyboy) <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> You can see the work in progress development wiki <a href=\"http://hunter-the-vigil-cults.wikia.com/wiki/Hunter_the_Vigil:_Cults_Wiki\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-26T03:10:22-08:00","id":18321,"title":"","content":"Cults? Hunters treading the edge of becoming what they fight? <i>PCs as part of a chain of command and not crazed rogue cowboys?</i> I think I'm in love, and I haven't even opened the link yet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-26T07:53:03-08:00","id":18407,"title":"","content":"If you want to contribute it's open development <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-26T22:56:03-08:00","id":18969,"title":"","content":"I knew homebrew would have come here soon enough just a matter of time and thanks","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/893-reaperfrost8","name":"reaperfrost8","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar893_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-29T04:14:14-08:00","id":20154,"title":"","content":"I added a link to London Underground (forgot about that one) my half finished city book for Geist. (It still needs the first half of the history and everything to do with the living half of the city, it started as a citybook for the Upper Reaches and sorta grew from there. In the unlikely event that anyone is interested in finishing it give me a shout).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-30T00:22:46-08:00","id":20530,"title":"","content":"I know they're a non-core Conspiracy, but you may wish to consider adding a bit on the VASCU for the Cults handbook. The FBI was a primary player in the Waco siege on the Branch Davidians, and maintain a handbook on cults and how to deal with them. In the World of Darkness, where cults are more common and sinister, the FBI's supernatural specialists would be well-versed in dealing with them.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-30T00:34:45-08:00","id":20532,"title":"","content":"VASCU aren't the FBI's supernatural specialists, they're the serial killer specialists. Since most Cults don't have any supernatural abilities it's probably the regular FBI that investigates them. Though maybe something like the Other Agencies sidebar on p54 would be a good idea. Want to write one? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-30T00:49:46-08:00","id":20537,"title":"","content":"I believe they loosely define &quot;slashers&quot; as any sort of supernatural serial criminal. That said, I could easily try my hand at writing something up. I feel like there was once a real Occult Crimes division, but I can't find anything on it.<br /> <br /> I'll shoot you a draft sometime very soon!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-30T02:06:00-08:00","id":20553,"title":"","content":"I recently had the opportunity to play a Princess in a very silly, rules-light game, but I still devoured the entire PDF for it and had a blast playing as a Grace in service of the Queen of Tears (secretly, of course). I was wondering if you're still tweaking that project, as I have a couple of ideas that might streamline a couple of things and would love to chat with you about it. I tried to send you a PM to this effect but the forums kept eating them up!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Cxuog44JenzbN7GaAyRqDO4DXce9VGv6ybaCv9yYsPk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Simulacre: An Alternative Morality Stat for Prometheans</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/9523-the-alchemy-lab-homebrew-athanors\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew Athanors</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/887-metamurpho","name":"Metamurpho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar887_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-30T02:28:15-08:00","id":20561,"title":"","content":"Would you by chance be one of PenDragon's players or are Princesses of Tears the new vogue for light hearted games <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I'd love to chat. I'll PM you my e-mail address.<br /> <br /> Edit, PMs aren't working for me either, but it's [redacted since Metamurpho has now seen my email<b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/887-metamurpho\">]</a></b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 11-30-2013, 07:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-21T20:02:56-07:00","id":96142,"title":"","content":"I just discovered this thread and your various homebrew settings. Though a number of them are interesting the Alchemy file you created made me sit up and go &quot;WOHA, I wants&quot;. So I was wondering if you had thought more about or anything.<br /> <br /> Basically, I really like the idea behind what that 'magic system' could do and I would love to read more about it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-22T01:48:16-07:00","id":96244,"title":"","content":"I haven't got anything for Alchemy other than the linked page.<br /> <br /> BTW, I noticed a few references to mortal Alchemists using Regent, those are all outdated. I'm going to get rid of them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-22T07:08:36-07:00","id":96327,"title":"","content":"So you listed 2 disney characters in the princess example concepts, but what would be the best x/y splat combinations for a disney ensemble team? And could mickey be a patron npc?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/885-bwgustaf","name":"bwgustaf","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"107"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-22T09:13:40-07:00","id":96370,"title":"","content":"Disney has so many characters that you can probably get away with any combination that you want. Though if you limit yourself purely to the official Disney Princess line then you've only got 13 too choose from, and a lot of the earlier ones are kind of similar. So here's my Disney Dream team, using TvTropes five man band as a template.<ul><li><a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/TheLeader\" target=\"_blank\">The Leader</a> \u2014 Kevin Flynn (Tron: Legacy). A Seeker of Diamonds, Embassy to the Dreamlands. Specialisms in Acqua and Legno; Learn and Govern. He's found an equivalent of the ISOs in the Dreamlands and put together an elite team to realize the opportunity. He's also partners with the Dreamlands reflection of himself.</li> <li><a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/TheLancer\" target=\"_blank\">The Lancer</a> \u2014 Fa Mulan (Mulan). A Champion of Spades. The most all rounded member of the team, always with another trick up her sleeve. Her leadership and level head make a useful balance to Flynn's introverted absentminded visionary. She can, and does, seize control of the team when she thinks Flynn is about to run off with a bad idea.</li> <li><a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/TheSmartGuy\" target=\"_blank\">The Smart Guy</a> \u2014 Milo Thatch (Atlantis: The Lost Empire). A Mender of Diamonds, Embassy to Machines. Though a trained linguist, Milo is an absolute natural with machines, able to quickly understand and repair devices from civilizations he's never seen before. Flynn wants to keep technological options, as well as Embassy priviliages, open. Plus the two geeks enjoy talking shop.</li> <li><a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/TheBigGuy\" target=\"_blank\">The Big Guy</a> \u2014 Merida (Brave). A Champion of Swords. Specializes in Fuoco but is beginning to learn Terra. After Blossoming Merida spent her time running wild and free, enjoying her magic but recently she has had a breakthrough in the relationship with her mother (a Grace of Hearts) and decided she needs to compromise between her wishes and her obligations. But her mother compromised too, and has allowed Merida a few more years of adventuring before she settles down.</li> <li><a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/TheChick\" target=\"_blank\">The Chick</a> \u2014 Wendy (Peter Pan). A Mender of Hearts. The youngest of the group, and something of a liability. They keep her because she has an enormous potential for working with the Dreamlands, and because Flynn sees her as an apprentice. What the others don't know, and she doesn't realize the significance of, is that she was taken by a True Fae. As a guest, not a prisoner, and her affinity for dreams is just one of the lasting effects of her trip to Arcadia.</li> </ul><br /> <br /> And yes, Mickey Mouse could be found in the Dreamlands and could be taken as a Mentor. A Shikigami is debatible. There's a upper limit on how powerful dreamlanders can be before they can become Shikigami (that's mostly there to justify why the Queens haven't done so themselves)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-22T09:43:38-07:00","id":96387,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrew-index?p=96370#post96370\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Disney has so many characters that you can probably get away with any combination that you want. Though if you limit yourself purely to the official Disney Princess line then you've only got 13 too choose from, and a lot of the earlier ones are kind of similar. So here's my Disney Dream team, using TvTropes five man band as a template.<ul><li><a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/TheLeader\" target=\"_blank\">The Leader</a> \u2014 Kevin Flynn (Tron: Legacy). A Seeker of Diamonds, Embassy to the Dreamlands. Specialisms in Acqua and Legno; Learn and Govern. He's found an equivalent of the ISOs in the Dreamlands and put together an elite team to realize the opportunity. He's also partners with the Dreamlands reflection of himself.</li> <li><a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/TheLancer\" target=\"_blank\">The Lancer</a> \u2014 Fa Mulan (Mulan). A Champion of Spades. The most all rounded member of the team, always with another trick up her sleeve. Her leadership and level head make a useful balance to Flynn's introverted absentminded visionary. She can, and does, seize control of the team when she thinks Flynn is about to run off with a bad idea.</li> <li><a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/TheSmartGuy\" target=\"_blank\">The Smart Guy</a> \u2014 Milo Thatch (Atlantis: The Lost Empire). A Mender of Diamonds, Embassy to Machines. Though a trained linguist, Milo is an absolute natural with machines, able to quickly understand and repair devices from civilizations he's never seen before. Flynn wants to keep technological options, as well as Embassy priviliages, open. Plus the two geeks enjoy talking shop.</li> <li><a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/TheBigGuy\" target=\"_blank\">The Big Guy</a> \u2014 Merida (Brave). A Champion of Swords. Specializes in Fuoco but is beginning to learn Terra. After Blossoming Merida spent her time running wild and free, enjoying her magic but recently she has had a breakthrough in the relationship with her mother (a Grace of Hearts) and decided she needs to compromise between her wishes and her obligations. But her mother compromised too, and has allowed Merida a few more years of adventuring before she settles down.</li> <li><a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/TheChick\" target=\"_blank\">The Chick</a> \u2014 Wendy (Peter Pan). A Mender of Hearts. The youngest of the group, and something of a liability. They keep her because she has an enormous potential for working with the Dreamlands, and because Flynn sees her as an apprentice. What the others don't know, and she doesn't realize the significance of, is that she was taken by a True Fae. As a guest, not a prisoner, and her affinity for dreams is just one of the lasting effects of her trip to Arcadia.</li> </ul><br /> <br /> <br /> And yes, Mickey Mouse could be found in the Dreamlands and could be taken as a Mentor. A Shikigami is debatible. There's a upper limit on how powerful dreamlanders can be before they can become Shikigami (that's mostly there to justify why the Queens haven't done so themselves)</div> </div> </div> </div>What about the 3 &quot;Classic&quot; Princesses (Belle, Cinderella, and Snow White)? Could they be slotted in the same category's of the smart girl, the leader, and the chick as princess archetypes?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/885-bwgustaf","name":"bwgustaf","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"107"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-22T09:53:43-07:00","id":96392,"title":"","content":"I think they'd all be The Chick. I haven't watched those ones for a while, but I don't remember any of them doing much except being nice people. Belle at least has her interest in books, but I don't think she ever made practical use of it or her father's inventions. Though you could always fix that if you Princessified Belle <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-24T17:40:02-07:00","id":97910,"title":"","content":"I never seen your Alchemy thing before! Is it unfinished? I don't see examples of things you could do with it, except for metaformulae. But it seems really Coolsville!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://