nly Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 05-15-2014, 02:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-21T01:02:44-07:00","id":144277,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/144244-alchymists-of-most-noble-good\">And they're up</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-06T18:15:28-07:00","id":161297,"title":"","content":"You once mentioned an Orthodox equivalent to the Malleus Maleficarum. Got any on them?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-06T23:13:04-07:00","id":161438,"title":"","content":"Sadly, no. I tried to give them a write up the other day and just got absolutely nowhere.<br /> <br /> <br /> It's the Order of St. Anthony (again, as a Conspiracy this time). The general gist is that they were founded by a Russian ghost. The Russian arm was suppressed and often killed by Stalin, most of the other arms were destroyed by the Nazis and they're now pulling themselves back together.<br /> <br /> Their Endowment is Benedictions, though with a sidebar encouraging you to give bonuses to defensive Benedictions to the Order; and offensive Benedictions to the MM if you want to distinguish them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-23T09:41:43-07:00","id":178020,"title":"","content":"<i><b>The Kings Raven</b></i>...<br /> <br /> Not sure if I ever asked you, but do you have any write-ups of NPC's lying around (Vampires in England would be keen) that could be cribbed for another game? After a while, My NPC's become a bit stale, and I am going through a creative dry spell.<br /> <br /> Thanks (whether or not you actually have anything). <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-23T10:07:44-07:00","id":178045,"title":"","content":"Not that many I'm afraid, and no Vampires as I'm not that interested in Requiem.<br /> <br /> I pretty much only write up NPCs when they're part of a wider project, Dream Catchers for example. NeoTiamat probably has some from his Walking Shadows game.<br /> <br /> <br /> Anyway; since I can't offer you NPCs, perhaps I can offer a tiny nugget of advice. In the UK really old things are far more common than in the USA, but they tend to be unremarkable and blend into the surroundings (heck, there was a house just down the road from me that's older than the USA). Consider the political cliamate that might allow an abudance of elders, yet each elder having the power of an ancilla.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-23T12:46:47-07:00","id":178135,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrew-index?p=178045#post178045\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not that many I'm afraid, and no Vampires as I'm not that interested in Requiem.<br /> <br /> I pretty much only write up NPCs when they're part of a wider project, Dream Catchers for example. NeoTiamat probably has some from his Walking Shadows game.<br /> <br /> <br /> Anyway; since I can't offer you NPCs, perhaps I can offer a tiny nugget of advice. In the UK really old things are far more common than in the USA, but they tend to be unremarkable and blend into the surroundings (heck, there was a house just down the road from me that's older than the USA). Consider the political cliamate that might allow an abudance of elders, yet each elder having the power of an ancilla.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ahh well... Thanks...No worries. Already cribbed a few of <i><b>NeoTiamat's </b></i>creations. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> Will keep that in mind. I have been doing some research, and though I am sure my American POV is rife with inaccuracies and potential prejudices, I continue to plug along. Though I am sure my city is a blending of both Old World and Colonial cross breading.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":540,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","user":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","date":". 06-23-2014, 03:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-23T12:57:08-07:00","id":178149,"title":"","content":"By the way, have you been 'researching' the UK's Being Human? Particularly season's 1-3?<br /> <br /> Though be warned I have heard some people say it is the final word on (angsty) vampire stories. Personally I think (and am very annoyed) at one little thread left dangling.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-23T13:48:34-07:00","id":178224,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrew-index?p=178149#post178149\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">By the way, have you been 'researching' the UK's Being Human? Particularly season's 1-3?<br /> <br /> Though be warned I have heard some people say it is the final word on (angsty) vampire stories. Personally I think (and am very annoyed) at one little thread left dangling.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have not... Actually been looking at Other Sources, none of which is popular entertainment media.<br /> Also looking at Newspapers and such, to get a feel of the day to day occurrences. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-23T14:09:52-07:00","id":178241,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=DGscoaUWW2M\" target=\"_blank\">Newspapers you say?</a><br /> <br /> <br /> You should give it a try. The UK has been having a boom in neat urban fantasy (though I think America has too). And it might be worth seeing if you can detect any noticeable differences that could be used in your games. <br /> <br /> Being Human and London Falling would be my go-to for example. Rivers of London is also ace, but a bit more light hearted than the WoD. You should also give Doctor Who a try, a lot of the leading lights in British urban fantasy worked on Doctor Who, and it's generally the most popular bit of British fantasy.<br /> <br /> Young Dracula might also be worth a look as another contemporary British vampire story, it is aimed at kids and can't go anywhere truly dark, it's still good and if it's not worth researching it's worth watching. Wolfblood is another good kids urban fantasy, but it doesn't have any vampires.<br /> <br /> <br /> I could talk in more general terms about British vs American urban fantasy; but if I'm honest it will be heavily biased by my tastes. It's not like I read dozens of books from each country to do a fair comparison. Though if you are interested in my biases just look at the Office of the Lord Stewards in Dream Catchers. Quite a few people said they didn't really fit in Hunter, which was kind of intentional - I wanted to push some boundaries so I based them on everything I perceived to be unique about British urban fantasy. I did create a hunter Conspiracy that can't carry guns and make a point of obeying that rule; that's not something I do without intent <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-23T15:11:05-07:00","id":178288,"title":"","content":"Awesome - Thanks, Will keep all that in mind. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-14T04:45:33-07:00","id":700681,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/691410-compact-ride-to-damascus-the-beastcrafters\">Just making sure this isn't forgotten. It's very good stuff.</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-14T09:37:54-07:00","id":700984,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the prod. It's now on the first page where it belongs <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-06T19:21:34-07:00","id":884256,"title":"","content":"Hi there,<br /> Long time lurker, first time poster, and I really love your stuff. I noticed you're working on Leviathan 2e, and loved Leviathan 1e to bits. So, I signed up for an account to ask:<br /> If you're looking for people to help on 2e, I'm more than happy to volunteer. I'm a GM of several years, and a technical writer by trade, so I'm happy to do layout and typesetting and compiling into a proper book, as well as playtesting with my group and hammering out any bugs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11740-diserasta","name":"Diserasta","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11740_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-06T23:48:14-07:00","id":884420,"title":"","content":"That's awesome <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I'd love volunteers. There's still lots of work to do before it's ready layout/typesetting/compiling, but I'd be delighted if you wanted to join the discussion or pitch ideas. I'd be especially interested in ideas for new Channels (the Attribute boosting Channels have been replaced with the new Atavism mechanics, so new Channels are needed to replace them), Hybrid Mutations or Rituals.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-07T00:14:14-07:00","id":884429,"title":"","content":"Well, I've got the 2E draft printed out here, and I'm just getting familiar with it. Will update this post with ideas in a bit.<br /> <br /> To make sure I've got things right, Atavisms are passive buffs that you get, while Channels are activated abilities that rely on Depth?<br /> <br /> Also, I'm going to be heavily critical below. I don't mean to attack you, but I do want to hammer out any problems, and that may come across aggressively. I apologise in advance.<br /> <br /> I'll leave grammatical and linguistical bugs out at this stage, unless they screw with the meaning.<br /> <br /> <b>Current Channels:</b><br /> <br /> Lambent Eyes, Depth 5: Another question could be, &quot;What is the most powerful emotion in the crowd?&quot; (A crowd could be inspired by a speaker, but a certain section could be disgusted by it) Alternatively, &quot;What fraction feel the strongest emotion, and what fraction feel the most common emotion?&quot;<br /> <br /> Eye of the Watchful Diety, Prophets Adaptation: Does this adaptation forgo the Breaking Point for the avatar, since they know they are a prophet? Should it? Should it provide a bonus to the Breaking Point roll if it still inflicts one?<br /> <br /> Eye of the Watchful Diety, All-Seeing Adaptation: This requires a total of eight dots to acquire (disregarding sheol cost), is this the intention?<br /> <br /> Uncrowned Fisher King, Depth 6: The 2e core has switched to metric. You can drop the miles per hour comparison, and simply have a conversion for kilometers per hour instead of meters per turn.<br /> <br /> Uncrowned Fisher King, Depth 7: What exactly is a &quot;reasonably sized river&quot;? Are we talking the Danube, or Rhine? Or the Nile? It's a good abstraction, but it provides no sense of scale. How about 10 times their Apotheosis Size, as defined by Sheol, in meters? Thus a Sheol 10 Leviathan would need a 550 meter wide river, and a Sheol 2 Leviathan would need a 30m wide river. Ref: <a href=\"https://www.gislounge.com/river-width-gis-data-created-from-1756-landsat-images/\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.gislounge.com/river-widt...andsat-images/</a> for river widths in NA. A Sheol 10 Leviathan could cross America causing only serious flooding in Central USA and the Canadian border. If you mean this to significantly restrict movement, we can go even higher.<br /> <br /> Echoes of the Deluge, Depth 2, Alternate Casting: Do you mean tech with Size smaller than Int + Science + Sheol dots? or do you mean roll, and count successes? Both are a little inelegant, but I can't think of a better way right now. Will return to this.<br /> <br /> Echoes of the Deluge, Depth 6: Flavourful, but ultimately kind of weak for a Depth 6 Channel embrace. Would broadening the class to &quot;anyone attempting to navigate in Tilts caused by this Channel&quot; work? That way it'll (usually) hit Sailors, as well as anyone you want to hinder. Your Beloved are already immune due to Depth 5 after all.<br /> <br /> Echoes of the Deluge, Depth 7, Tribute to Tiamat: Could offering the sacrifice generate one Ichor per person if individual, or five Ichor (or ten, I'm not sure what you want the balance of economy to be like) for a group offering? Does this make it too powerful?<br /> <br /> Swallowing the Sun, Depth 5: It's never established that the Leviathan is immune to the Tilt generated by this Channel? Are Leviathans generally immune to their Channels, or should it be clarified here?<br /> <br /> Mother of a Thousand Young, Depth 3: You note &quot;additional Ichor&quot;. Do you mean Ichor besides activation cost, or does generating a first-degree spawn cost Ichor? If it does, either the general description, or Depth 1 should be updated.<br /> <br /> I need to do a second pass, but this is what I've found so far.<br /> <br /> <b>New Channels:</b><br /> <br /> A lot of these powers focus on the horrifying aspects of Lovecraftian monstrosities, but a Tranquil Leviathan knows her Beloved are people, and treats them as such. They may be a tad clinical, or prone to outbursts, but they mean well. Gods can still care for their subjects. This may be out of flavour, but I enjoy the thought of Leviathans struggling to be &quot;good people&quot;.<br /> <br /> Nothing comes to mind immediately, but I'll mull over it. Something that empowers their Beloved maybe? Or avoids the mind-breaking aspects of being Beloved, so their cults aren't full of insane people? Maybe moves the burden to the Leviathan? It would be looked down upon as denigrating their divine nature, but it would allow their Beloved some <i>semblance </i>of sanity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11740,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11740-diserasta","user":"Diserasta","date":".  More thoughts on new stuff 05-07-2016, 04:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11740-diserasta","name":"Diserasta","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11740_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-07T01:10:52-07:00","id":884456,"title":"","content":"Not quite. Atavaisms are extra dots you get to Attributes while Transformed. Channels can be active or passive but provide more complex abilities than simply giving you extra Dots or dice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-07T01:42:50-07:00","id":884469,"title":"","content":"Understood. I've updated the post above with current thoughts. Looking forward to see your thoughts on things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11740-diserasta","name":"Diserasta","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11740_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-07T03:19:54-07:00","id":884503,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Diserasta</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrew-index?p=884429#post884429\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lambent Eyes, Depth 5: Another question could be, &quot;What is the most powerful emotion in the crowd?&quot; (A crowd could be inspired by a speaker, but a certain section could be disgusted by it) Alternatively, &quot;What fraction feel the strongest emotion, and what fraction feel the most common emotion?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div> Good ideas.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Diserasta</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrew-index?p=884429#post884429\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Eye of the Watchful Diety, Prophets Adaptation: Does this adaptation forgo the Breaking Point for the avatar, since they know they are a prophet? Should it? Should it provide a bonus to the Breaking Point roll if it still inflicts one?</div> </div> </div> </div> I've been meaning to remove the Breaking Point from Eye entirely. As most Beloved are faceless extras a breaking point feels like unnecessary bookkeeping.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Diserasta</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrew-index?p=884429#post884429\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Eye of the Watchful Diety, All-Seeing Adaptation: This requires a total of eight dots to acquire (disregarding sheol cost), is this the intention?</div> </div> </div> </div> That was the intent. do you think it's too high?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Diserasta</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrew-index?p=884429#post884429\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Uncrowned Fisher King, Depth 6: The 2e core has switched to metric. You can drop the miles per hour comparison, and simply have a conversion for kilometers per hour instead of meters per turn.</div> </div> </div> </div> Good point. To the calculator.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Diserasta</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrew-index?p=884429#post884429\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Uncrowned Fisher King, Depth 7: What exactly is a &quot;reasonably sized river&quot;?</div> </div> </div> </div> I have long since given up trying to make any sense of what WoD's &quot;Size&quot; actually means, but I think I'd prefer a flat size rather than one that varies depending on Sheol. In 2E I'm trying to move away from &quot;you can't do this&quot; to &quot;you can do this, but it will have consiquences&quot;.<br /> <br /> So perhaps say 30 meters, I based it on the Thames as it's a river I know well and it felt about right. That said, if a Leviathan did swim into central London flooding everything they would surely find a lot of enemies waiting for them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Diserasta</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrew-index?p=884429#post884429\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Echoes of the Deluge, Depth 2, Alternate Casting: Do you mean tech with Size smaller than Int + Science + Sheol dots? or do you mean roll, and count successes?</div> </div> </div> </div> The first.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Diserasta</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrew-index?p=884429#post884429\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Echoes of the Deluge, Depth 6: Flavourful, but ultimately kind of weak for a Depth 6 Channel embrace. Would broadening the class to &quot;anyone attempting to navigate in Tilts caused by this Channel&quot; work? That way it'll (usually) hit Sailors, as well as anyone you want to hinder.</div> </div> </div> </div> I know it's a little weak, but I wouldn't want to dilute the flavour.<br /> <br /> A better idea would probably to add a second effect to make up for it being a little weak. Of course that requires thinking up a second effect.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Diserasta</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrew-index?p=884429#post884429\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Echoes of the Deluge, Depth 7, Tribute to Tiamat: Could offering the sacrifice generate one Ichor per person if individual, or five Ichor (or ten, I'm not sure what you want the balance of economy to be like) for a group offering? Does this make it too powerful?</div> </div> </div> </div> I think a point Ichor for the first sacrifice in a scene would be safe. (That Adaptation is a sneaky one that mostly exists for non-Leviathan games with a Leviathan antagonist.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Diserasta</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrew-index?p=884429#post884429\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Swallowing the Sun, Depth 5: It's never established that the Leviathan is immune to the Tilt generated by this Channel? Are Leviathans generally immune to their Channels, or should it be clarified here?</div> </div> </div> </div> At some point I plan to write an opening section to the Vestage of Elements that lays out Leviathans' immunity to their own effects.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Diserasta</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrew-index?p=884429#post884429\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mother of a Thousand Young, Depth 3: You note &quot;additional Ichor&quot;. Do you mean Ichor besides activation cost, or does generating a first-degree spawn cost Ichor? If it does, either the general description, or Depth 1 should be updated.</div> </div> </div> </div> First degrees cost Ichor.<br /> <br /> Thanks for this, I'm now going to update the scrapbook with these.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Diserasta</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrew-index?p=884429#post884429\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Something that empowers their Beloved maybe?</div> </div> </div> </div> You'll be glad to know that's on it's way <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> (It's Rituals though, not Channels. Though The Hydra's Rebirth does allow healing)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Diserasta</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrew-index?p=884429#post884429\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or avoids the mind-breaking aspects of being Beloved, so their cults aren't full of insane people?</div> </div> </div> </div>This one I'm going to say no too, at least not as a Channel.<br /> <br /> Making Beloved saner would be like removing the need for Vampire's to drink blood. Requium <i>does</i> provide ways for Vampire's to reduce their blood dependency - but they're hidden in corners like Coils of the Dragon or Invictiucs blood oaths.<br /> <br /> Anything Leviathans do to help their beloved become sane would have to be similar. Not a Channel, but some thing weirder and harder to find.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 05-07-2016, 06:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-07T06:22:05-07:00","id":884578,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11740-diserasta\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar11740_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11740\" data-vbnamecard=\"11740\">Diserasta</a> Channels also seem to be more about personal power, while Rituals are about group workings. Something to &quot;de-insanify&quot; cult members would probably be a Ritual performed monthly, or as directed by their doctor/cult-leader.<br /> <br /> Though I did have notes on an Evolution that let the Leviathan create a kind of &quot;snap-shot&quot; spirit/goetic/whatever of people pre-Beloved, which they used give their cultists a kind of &quot;sane advisor&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-07T07:18:42-07:00","id":884598,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrew-index?p=884578#post884578\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11740-diserasta\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar11740_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11740\" data-vbnamecard=\"11740\">Diserasta</a> Channels also seem to be more about personal power, while Rituals are about group workings. Something to &quot;de-insanify&quot; cult members would probably be a Ritual performed monthly, or as directed by their doctor/cult-leader.<br /> <br /> Though I did have notes on an Evolution that let the Leviathan create a kind of &quot;snap-shot&quot; spirit/goetic/whatever of people pre-Beloved, which they used give their cultists a kind of &quot;sane advisor&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>An Evolution could be cool. Stop them from being so incredibly ineffective at life. :P<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrew-index?p=884503#post884503\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Good ideas.<br /> I have long since given up trying to make any sense of what WoD's &quot;Size&quot; actually means, but I think I'd prefer a flat size rather than one that varies depending on Sheol. In 2E I'm trying to move away from &quot;you can't do this&quot; to &quot;you can do this, but it will have consiquences&quot;.<br /> <br /> So perhaps say 30 meters, I based it on the Thames as it's a river I know well and it felt about right. That said, if a Leviathan did swim into central London flooding everything they would surely find a lot of enemies waiting for them..</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, Size is a tad nebulous. Wish I had a better system, but none really comes to mind. Ars Magica's Size system is less nebulous, where Size is a good scale sense, but it's an exponential system. (Size -8 is a single ant, Size -4 is a robin, Size -2 is a cat, Size -1 is a large dog, or a human child, Size 0 is adult human, Size 1 is big dude, Size 3 is war horse, Size 5 is elephant, Size 9 is blue whale) It's a bit too ugly for use in a system where everything else scales linearly for the most part.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrew-index?p=884503#post884503\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This one I'm going to say no too, at least not as a Channel.<br /> <br /> Making Beloved saner would be like removing the need for Vampire's to drink blood. Requium <i>does</i> provide ways for Vampire's to reduce their blood dependency - but they're hidden in corners like Coils of the Dragon or Invictiucs blood oaths.<br /> <br /> Anything Leviathans do to help their beloved become sane would have to be similar. Not a Channel, but some thing weirder and harder to find.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair enough. That's a good point, and I agree. The cults need to be insane because that's how they function on a fundamental level, and because it's how they generate Ichor (through veneration).<br /> I originally had a different thought in mind (companions, in the style of Claudia and Lestrade to Louis), but I imagine that's what Atolls are designed to be. Something that inexorably draws you in, and yet has the potential to destroy you.<br /> <br /> Related, will there be any way for Leviathans to stabalise their Tranquility? Vampires have Touchstones, for example. Is there any plan for a similar system, or are Leviathans designed to be more volatile? Atolls do have a stabilising effect, in that they directly modify Phronesis and Euonia, but they're incredibly dangerous too.<br /> <br /> I'll post again once I do second run of the rules.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11740,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11740-diserasta","user":"Diserasta","date":". 05-07-2016, 10:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11740-diserasta","name":"Diserasta","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11740_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-07T07:25:16-07:00","id":884600,"title":"","content":"Maybe we should take this discussion to the Leviathan thread. But in answer to your question, I haven't read Interview with a Vampire but it sounds like you've got a good grasp on what Atolls are meant to be.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-07T07:27:01-07:00","id":884601,"title":"","content":"There's a Leviathan thread? Well, TIL, we should definitely move there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11740-diserasta","name":"Diserasta","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11740_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-07T07:49:29-07:00","id":884622,"title":"","content":"A link: forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/434590-leviathan-the-cult-chronicles","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-05T08:25:34-07:00","id":907647,"title":"","content":"So, I'm sorry if I shouldn't have asked this here, but I figured it made the most sense to do so... having bitten the bullet and finally looked at Princess the Hopeful, I need to ask; what's the difference between the Dream and Vocation versions? What's the underlying thematic difference that caused the two versions to be split? Neither the Wiki nor the TVTropes article really makes any explanation of it, and if there's a difference between the two in the books, I've missed it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5487-voiddrifter","name":"VoidDrifter","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-05T09:44:17-07:00","id":907682,"title":"","content":"The origonal split was mostly because we couldn't get anything done at all without arguing forever over details; and there's lots of small differences everywhere. The biggest thematic difference is that in Vocation Princesses strongly tied to Princess led organisations (called Camaraderies); autologous to the Mage's Consillia. In Dream Princess specific social groups beyond the Nakama level are uncommon; instead Princesses tie themselves to mortal groups like Greenpeace or a political party.<br /> <br /> Vocation is also supposed to be a game about war stories (through that includes things like M*A*S*H). Actually... I'm not sure if that's still the intent. Meanwhile Dream is supposed to tell any story that starts with &quot;you're idealistic and you suddenly gain power, what do you do next?&quot;. If that means magical community activists set in The Wire's Baltimore - Dream should support it.<br /> <br /> (Obviously this post is from a Dream centric perspective. Tagging in <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1133-michael-brazier\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1133\" data-vbnamecard=\"1133\">Michael Brazier</a> so he can give his side of the story).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-05T12:45:32-07:00","id":907802,"title":"","content":"Since you are so obliging ...<br /> <br /> My objection to Kings Raven's take on Princess was, basically, that it deemphasized or denatured the fantastical and supernatural parts of the game. The Camaraderie thing is the best example of both, though it came after the split. In the Dream version Hopeful social groups above the nakama level are located only in the Dreamlands - which has the double effect of removing such groups from any concerns local to an area, and of changing the Dreamlands from a setting for adventures into a knockoff of an Internet forum. Neither IMO is desirable.<br /> <br /> Another instance is the different Echo rules. In Dream a Princess' Echo is an innate Inspiring Merit. In Vocation it's an <i>aura</i> - like the predatory aura of vampires, the hunter's aspect of werewolves and the nimbus of mages; you can use it to oppose other auras. There's a definite difference between a Princess being generally an example to others, and a Princess reaching into her better self to resist a vampire's seduction; the latter is more obviously supernatural than the former.<br /> <br /> I've always found it amusing that Vocation has actual rules for Princesses playing mundane politics and tying themselves to mundane groups, while Dream (where such things are supposedly the most frequent concern) doesn't really have anything to support it, even Storyteller advice on exploiting the CofD mechanics for that purpose. But that's not a thematic difference, just KR not liking those rules very much. And really, most of the differences between the versions are mechanics, not themes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1133-michael-brazier","name":"Michael Brazier","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-05T13:19:45-07:00","id":907825,"title":"","content":"I was expecting you to disagree more with what I said. You describe Dream as &quot;deemphasizing the supernatural&quot; but I'd describe vocation as deemphasizing the mundane. And if there's any WoD gameline where, E.G., police corruption should be an issue that matters to the protagonists it's Princesses. In Dream a Princess playing the Harry Dresden to a SI division is a very valid concept. In Vocation, why bother working with mortal society when you've got a Camandarie instead? I don't agree with your point about the Dreamlands though. The fact that Princesses use their Queen's palaces as an internet forum doesn't stop the other 99% of the Dreamlands being a place for adventures.<br /> <br /> Re: Echos. From my viewpoint the difference is that by making Vocation's Echo's an at-will activated ability it reduces a Princess' Virtue down to a catchphrase. In Dream if a Princess fulfils her Virtue it inspires everyone around her. In Vocation if a Princess shouts &quot;In the name of the Moon, I will punish you&quot; it inspires everyone. That's not a thematic statement about who Princesses are or who this Princess is. That's just another Charm.<br /> <br /> As for Nations. I dislike giving organisations stat blocks, IMO it takes the focus away from the characters instead. And, well, Vampire never needed organisation rules to make political games.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-05T13:37:14-07:00","id":907841,"title":"","content":"I see. Thank you both for clarifying. You might want to make it clearer in the docs which version is which - for example, titling the PDFs &quot;Princess the Hopeful(V or D)&quot; and adding a short paragraph noting which version it is and why in the intro. Right now, I have no real way of being sure I have both versions of the doc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5487-voiddrifter","name":"VoidDrifter","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-05T13:50:39-07:00","id":907848,"title":"","content":"Maybe someday you\u00b4ll find the time and the inspiration to go back to Mage the Indebted and turn it into a major splat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-05T14:02:26-07:00","id":907859,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Raistlin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrew-index?p=907848#post907848\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe someday you\u00b4ll find the time and the inspiration to go back to Mage the Indebted and turn it into a major splat.</div> </div> </div> </div>That was I think my earliest bit of homebrew. It's not finished and I haven't looked at it in ages, but I imagine it's not up to the standards of my more recent work. But there's plenty of material... digs... digs... <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/MageTheIndebted0.3.5.1.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 06-05-2016, 05:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-05T14:31:37-07:00","id":907887,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrew-index?p=907859#post907859\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That was I think my earliest bit of homebrew. It's not finished and I haven't looked at it in ages, but I imagine it's not up to the standards of my more recent work. But there's plenty of material... digs... digs... <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/MageTheIndebted0.3.5.1.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a></div> </div> </div> </div>Hipster Indebted<i>: I was making &quot;Goblin Vows&quot; before they were cool.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2411,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","user":"Raistlin","date":". 06-05-2016, 05:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-05T17:36:35-07:00","id":908001,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrew-index?p=907825#post907825\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was expecting you to disagree more with what I said. You describe Dream as &quot;deemphasizing the supernatural&quot; but I'd describe vocation as deemphasizing the mundane. And if there's any WoD gameline where, E.G., police corruption should be an issue that matters to the protagonists it's Princesses. In Dream a Princess playing the Harry Dresden to a SI division is a very valid concept. In Vocation, why bother working with mortal society when you've got a Camandarie instead?</div> </div> </div> </div>Unless police corruption has become a true city-wide emergency, most of the Princesses in the city will be dealing with other problems, more suited to their particular talents. Having a Camaraderie doesn't change that. In Vocation a single Camaraderie does not cover the whole of a Princess' social life, or the whole of her duties as a Princess - its purpose is mutual support in the face of supernatural problems all Princesses have, such as not being eaten by zombies. This is explicitly stated in the text, by the way.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrew-index?p=907825#post907825\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Re: Echos. From my viewpoint the difference is that by making Vocation's Echo's an at-will activated ability it reduces a Princess' Virtue down to a catchphrase. In Dream if a Princess fulfils her Virtue it inspires everyone around her. In Vocation if a Princess shouts &quot;In the name of the Moon, I will punish you&quot; it inspires everyone.</div> </div> </div> </div>It wouldn't work as an aura if it weren't activated at will. And making the Echo an aura says a Princess' Virtue is inspirational even in its smaller manifestations, whereas Dream's rule restricts when Virtue inspires others to the times she would normally gain Willpower from it. You made Virtues more potent; I made them come up more often.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrew-index?p=907825#post907825\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for Nations. I dislike giving organisations stat blocks, IMO it takes the focus away from the characters instead.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do you also dislike giving NPCs stat blocks, because that takes the focus away from the PCs? 99% of the time an organization in play is controlled by the Storyteller.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1133-michael-brazier","name":"Michael Brazier","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-06T02:22:34-07:00","id":908212,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael Brazier</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrew-index?p=908001#post908001\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">its purpose is mutual support in the face of supernatural problems all Princesses have, such as not being eaten by zombies. This is explicitly stated in the text, by the way.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just to check, you are aware that the SI division is specifically for investigating supernatural crimes?<br /> <br /> Because your reply is just resating what I said. I said a Princess should be worried about the Police force being corrupt because if a Princess wants backup against supernatural threats training the police force into Hunters is a sensible choice. In Vocation why would she worry about the police force when she can just go to the Camandarie instead?<br /> <br /> Same goes for the local journalists (Sailor Truth represent!). Making allies and contacts with the local journalists would be a good way to keep track of Taint or new Blossomings. In Vocation that role is made obsolete by a Camandarie. Same goes for social services - they'd be a good source of information on Taint. But in Vocation, if they're underfunded or corrupt you could just go to your Camandarie instead.<br /> <br /> In Dream, a Champion who's goal is to hunt down Darkspawn will probably be working closely with mundane society. In Vocation, a Darkspawn hunter will be working with a Princess founded and led Camandarie. It downplays and marginalises the role of mortal society in the gameline where mortal society should be more important than any other.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael Brazier</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrew-index?p=908001#post908001\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> You made Virtues more potent; I made them come up more often.</div> </div> </div> </div> ...That's exactly what I said.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael Brazier</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrew-index?p=908001#post908001\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you also dislike giving NPCs stat blocks, because that takes the focus away from the PCs?</div> </div> </div> </div> Don't be absurd. NPC stat blocks exist on the same level of play as PCs. Organisations are an entirely seperate level of play.<br /> <br /> <br /> BTW. We missed out the biggest thematic difference. In Vocation a Princess is mechanically penalised for doing magic in front of mundane witnesses by taking the Tracked Condition. Basically, if you do magic in public you will get a monster going after your friends (at a minimum). In Dream you don't get any such consiquences unless you screw up and leave behind evidence pointing to your secret identity or your allies' identities.<br /> <br /> Again this comes down to the core difference. Dream encourages you to interact with mundane society; Vocation encourages you to interact with hidden supernatural society.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-06T08:38:43-07:00","id":908358,"title":"","content":"Well, that's the thing. Stories in which a small group of magically-empowered friends, advised by an equally magical mentor, defeat a world-threatening evil with their magic powers are a dime a dozen in manga and anime. Stories where the magical heroes are the tip of a big but basically mundane organization, where mundane support plays a significant role in the plot? It's <i>much</i> harder to find examples from Japan; the ones that come to mind naturally are from American comics, or the pulps they descended from. The Dream version drifts the setting to Western superhero tropes; Vocation's take stays near the magical girl genre.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1133-michael-brazier","name":"Michael Brazier","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-06T10:06:14-07:00","id":908410,"title":"","content":"In the very first episode of Vividred Operation magical girls fight side by side with an entire naval task force; and after that they're officially inducted into the military. In Mai-OTOME magical girls replaced conventional military, and considerable mundane resources are spent on running the magical girl training school. In Mahou no Tenshi Creamy Mami, Mami gets has a mundane producer backing her. Then there's Nahona where a quick google search suggests that the TSAB is the openly acknowledged government of several worlds. Even Sailor Moon, well she ends up as the queen of Earth. How much more mundane backing can you get?<br /> <br /> So, being backed by a mundane organisation is not the standard format for magical girls, but it's hardly unkown. It's Camaraderies that lack precedent. When magical girl organisations scale up, they don't form secret societies. They integrate into or rule over mundane society. Dream just assumes they do so without being overt about the magic, since this is the WoD.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 06-06-2016, 01:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-06T12:34:38-07:00","id":908518,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrew-index?p=908410#post908410\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the very first episode of Vividred Operation magical girls fight side by side with an entire naval task force; and after that they're officially inducted into the military. In Mai-OTOME magical girls replaced conventional military, and considerable mundane resources are spent on running the magical girl training school. In Mahou no Tenshi Creamy Mami, Mami gets has a mundane producer backing her. Then there's Nahona where a quick google search suggests that the TSAB is the openly acknowledged government of several worlds. Even Sailor Moon, well she ends up as the queen of Earth. How much more mundane backing can you get?</div> </div> </div> </div>Vividred Operation has a magic power plant supplying electricity to most of Japan as a central plot point; Mai-Otome is set in the distant future on a lost colony world; after the first two seasons the Nanoha franchise leaves Earth entirely for worlds ruled by the TSAB; Sailor Moon doesn't become queen of Earth during the story proper, but sometime in the future; and Creamy Mami is a singer on a concert tour, not a political figure. Mami's the only one of your examples that has serious support from a mundane organization <i>and</i> is living on modern Earth, and the scope of her story is strictly personal.<br /> <br /> In fact, with respect to modern Earth the TSAB actually <i>is</i> a secret society, like the Camaraderie idea, during the first two Nanoha seasons. No one affiliated with the Bureau ever thinks of enlisting the help of Earth's governments to chase down the Jewel Seeds or the Wolkenritter, or of looking for mundane recruits on Earth. They assume jurisdiction over Nanoha and Hayate, based entirely on their knowledge of magic (as the TSAB doesn't rule Earth in any sense.) And while several TSAB members reside on Earth for years, they carefully conceal the fact that they came from other planets from anyone who doesn't already know. In short, they act almost exactly as the usual WoD/CofD supernatural conspiracies do, as long as the franchise stays on Earth.<br /> <br /> The standard situation in the Dream version is, I repeat, much more of a Western pulp/superhero trope. It's Doc Savage and his close advisors, the Shadow and his network of informants, Batman and his &quot;family&quot; of vigilantes, Buffy Summers and her high school friends. You don't get that trope with magical girls. (One reason for that, I think, is that to be plausible it almost requires the protagonist to have a fair chunk of experience before the story starts; that is, to be functionally an adult. By definition magical girls are <i>not</i> adults. Thus if a magical girl is supposed to use a network of mundane allies to deal with her troubles, much of her story has to be spent on her recruiting those allies, decreasing the time available for magical fireworks.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1133-michael-brazier","name":"Michael Brazier","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-06T13:54:45-07:00","id":908579,"title":"","content":"Where it's set is irrelevant. You can't just arbitrarily ignore precedent any show that disagrees with your pre-decided conclusion.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael Brazier</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrew-index?p=908518#post908518\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thus if a magical girl is supposed to use a network of mundane allies to deal with her troubles, much of her story has to be spent on her recruiting those allies, decreasing the time available for magical fireworks.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh no! Princesses spend an equal amount of time winning love by daylight and fighting evil by moonlight. It's working exactly as I intended, whatever shall I do?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-06T18:38:45-07:00","id":908781,"title":"","content":"When a society knows all about magic and uses it freely (all your examples save Creamy Mami) the ways that magical girls interact with it will obviously be different from what they'd do in the CofD setting, where magic is generally feared and ignored. Hence most of your examples prove nothing; indeed, the Nanoha franchise, during the part actually set on Earth, is against your claim.<br /> <br /> Again, the issue with Dream's setup is that it says &quot;Princesses eventually become Doc Savage&quot;, and magical girls ... just don't become Doc Savage. Seriously, I've never heard of a manga or anime that could be described that way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1133-michael-brazier","name":"Michael Brazier","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-06T23:47:50-07:00","id":908934,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael Brazier</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrew-index?p=908781#post908781\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When a society knows all about magic and uses it freely the ways that magical girls interact with it will obviously be different from what they'd do in the CofD setting where magic is generally feared and ignored. Hence most of your examples prove nothing</div> </div> </div> </div> It doesn't work that way. When the precedent doesn't match the setting, you don't ignore it, you take the underlying ideas and adapt them.<br /> <br /> The underlying ideas is that magical girls work with mundane society. When magic is feared and ignored that means they still work with mundane society, but they keep the magic quiet.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael Brazier</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrew-index?p=908781#post908781\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(all your examples save Creamy Mami)</div> </div> </div> </div> And Vividred Operation. It's set in the future, but not very far in the future. The setting is more our world than not. The Materialization engine is public, but the fact it can be used for &quot;magic&quot; is not.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael Brazier</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrew-index?p=908781#post908781\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Again, the issue with Dream's setup is that it says &quot;Princesses eventually become Doc Savage&quot;, and magical girls ... just don't become Doc Savage. Seriously, I've never heard of a manga or anime that could be described that way.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't even know where you're getting Doc Savage from. That's just a strawman argument.<br /> <br /> If you look at the examples I gave there's no unofficial alliance of advisors. It's usually an official public organisation. Creamy Mami and her music producers. Vividred Operation and the military.<br /> <br /> Camaraderies are far closer to Doc Savage than the basically-Creamy Mami's music producers Principalities. (in fact, I should add that example to the PDF. It is one of the most famous)<br /> <br /> [edit]<br /> I know we could go on for weeks. But I think this has answered VoidDrifter's question. If you want Princesses to work with mundane institutions and have an equal focus on winning love by daylight and fighting evil by moonlight; go for dream. if you want Princesses to work in secret supernatural institutions and focus on &quot;magical fireworks&quot; go for Vocation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 06-07-2016, 03:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T18:23:18-07:00","id":957967,"title":"","content":"Hello, I am new to the forums and would like to ask a question of you if that is alright. Since you are one of the primary authors perhaps you can explain why Princess doesn't have its own specialized hunter group. Yes I know there are the Storm-Wracked but they aren't specific like others. Was it word count or just unnecessary? I would also like to ask for permission to post an idea for such a compact onto the forums if that is okay.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12243-dreaming-cat","name":"Dreaming Cat","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"30"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T20:41:37-07:00","id":958035,"title":"","content":"Not <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar134_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"134\" data-vbnamecard=\"134\">The Kings Raven</a>, but if I recall, Princesses get grouped in with Mages by many Hunters.<br /> <br /> Barring that, it take a special kind of jerk to hunt magical girls just trying to bring hope, doesn't it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T22:47:51-07:00","id":958071,"title":"","content":"I think what you're asking is why nobody wrote a Princess focused Hunter: the Vigil suppliment? The answer is because no one got around to writing them.<br /> <br /> My concept was a public relations firm that won a high profile election against a Noble candidate and got famous as the go-to firm for Noble releated issues. If you're trying to win an election against a Grace or dealing with a Seeker publishing your companies shady deals you hire them. They specalise in charachter assassinations and investigations, they're not above blackmailing a Princess by threatening to make her mundane identity public either (though if they've found it chances are supernatural foes already know) but they bend rather than break the law and have basically no combat assets.<br /> <br /> Oh, and you don't need permission to post your concepts. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-27T18:40:02-07:00","id":959006,"title":"","content":"Thank you TKR. I did not want to anger anyone by treading on their creations. My idea was less of a group focused on magical girls than one focused on the Darkness. Essentially they're teachers whose desire to protect their students reached a peak when they noticed said students fighting evil by moonlight. Now they put Nobles on the sidelines, forcibly if needed, to keep them safe. Think a cross between Marvel's Punisher and Ms. Frizzle if that helps.<br /> <br /> Also <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar7212_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"7212\" data-vbnamecard=\"7212\">Vent0</a>, haven't the forces of Alhambra been sucking the literal hope and joy from the world for centuries? I could have sworn that was noticed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12243-dreaming-cat","name":"Dreaming Cat","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"30"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-27T23:31:34-07:00","id":959119,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dreaming Cat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrew-index?p=959006#post959006\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Think a cross between Marvel's Punisher and Ms. Frizzle if that helps.</div> </div> </div> </div> That's not a sentence I expected to be reading.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dreaming Cat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrew-index?p=959006#post959006\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar7212_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"7212\" data-vbnamecard=\"7212\">Vent0</a>, haven't the forces of Alhambra been sucking the literal hope and joy from the world for centuries? I could have sworn that was noticed.</div> </div> </div> </div>They have.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-28T04:31:06-07:00","id":959172,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrew-index?p=959119#post959119\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> That's not a sentence I expected to be reading.<br /> <br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> After reading Alan Moore\u00b4s version of Mary Poppins, I\u00b4m not even fazed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}